WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.600
Would a true friend leave their&nbsp;
pal behind in a hot steam tunnel?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:09.120
With rats? Apparently to die? Some "Big Bang&nbsp;
Theory" fans say the answer is a clear "no."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:11.920
Here's the scene that has them steaming mad.

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:14.960
While "The Big Bang Theory" may be a comedy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:18.880
its 12 seasons include a few&nbsp;
moments capable of inciting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:23.680
strong, angry reactions from some viewers.&nbsp;
Many of these scenes happen to involve Raj&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:28.080
Koothrappali and his poor treatment at the hands&nbsp;
of those closest to him throughout the series.

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:29.760
"I thought we were best friends!"

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:33.600
"We are! That's why I'm sad my&nbsp;
best friend's gonna be homeless."

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:38.000
At first glance, Raj and his science-minded&nbsp;
buddies Sheldon Cooper, Leonard Hofstadter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:42.560
and Howard Wolowitz appear to be a tight-knit&nbsp;
foursome. On numerous occasions, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:47.440
Raj is made to feel left out from the group.&nbsp;
This is especially true when Sheldon, Leonard,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:53.120
and Howard begin dating Amy Farrah Fowler, Penny,&nbsp;
and Bernadette Rostenkowski, respectively. Before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:56.880
long, they then start abandoning Raj to&nbsp;
spend more time with their girlfriends.

00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:01.440
Raj, on the other hand, has horrible luck&nbsp;
with women. One romantic interest of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:05.840
even climbed out of a window to escape&nbsp;
from him on a date. If that wasn't enough,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:10.560
"The Big Bang Theory" concludes with each of&nbsp;
its main characters enjoying a happy ending,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:15.440
except for Raj, that is. Though he revels&nbsp;
in bringing "Buffy the Vampire Slayer" star&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:20.160
Sarah Michelle Gellar to Sheldon and Amy's&nbsp;
Nobel Prize ceremony, she sets the terms:

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:22.566
"Just to be clear, this isn't a date."

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:23.620
"I know."

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:26.080
"Then why are you holding my hand?"

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:30.880
While fans of Raj surely feel for him in&nbsp;
each of these and similar occurrences,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:35.840
one particular conflict between him and&nbsp;
Sheldon had his fans truly seeing red.

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:41.200
In an episode in the eighth season, Sheldon and&nbsp;
Raj aspire to participate in a government-funded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:45.360
experiment on dark matter. As it turns&nbsp;
out, it involves staying in a tiny,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:50.800
100-degree-fahrenheit salt mine for&nbsp;
a total of 12 hours. To prepare,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:54.560
Sheldon and Raj conduct a simulation&nbsp;
within the steam tunnels of CalTech.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:59.280
Though Sheldon walks confidently into the&nbsp;
experience, he quickly becomes claustrophobic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:04.480
once it's underway. Raj then tries to calm him&nbsp;
by recounting the history of "Hannah Montana."

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:07.360
"...but then she would take off her wig&nbsp;
and go to school like a normal girl,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:10.400
which I don't have to tell you,&nbsp;
at that age, is its own headache."&nbsp;

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:16.320
Sheldon's breaking point comes 11 minutes into the&nbsp;
ordeal, when he spots two massive rats behind Raj,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:21.200
prompting him to abruptly leave his supposed&nbsp;
friend behind. Sheldon flees upstairs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:26.240
slams the tunnel's door shut, and informs&nbsp;
lookout Amy that it's "too late" for Raj.

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:30.320
The episode ends with a sweaty,&nbsp;
frazzled Raj confronting Sheldon:

00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:31.920
"You call yourself a friend?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:37.120
I was trying to help you and at the&nbsp;
first sign of trouble, you ran away!"

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:39.680
A number of fans were angered by the CalTech steam&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:42.800
tunnel situation after watching&nbsp;
it unfold. One Redditor wrote,

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:46.480
"I feel like they treated Raj like&nbsp;
s--- for a lot of the show. His dad&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:50.720
was right in the last season when he told&nbsp;
him his friendship with them was toxic."

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:51.600
Another wrote,

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:56.240
"[Sheldon] doesn't just leave him there&nbsp;
he actually closes the metal hatch door."

00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:59.920
Another Redditor pointed out that Amy&nbsp;
doesn't even attempt to reopen the hatch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:04.240
door and help Raj escape, despite&nbsp;
seeming fully capable of doing so.

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:08.560
Contrary to his character's poor treatment&nbsp;
on "The Big Bang Theory," actor Kunal Nayyar,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:12.800
who played Raj, has assured fans that&nbsp;
he and the real-life cast of "The Big&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:17.520
Bang Theory" are on good terms. Speaking to&nbsp;
HeyUGuys, Nayyar had nothing but the highest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:22.000
praise for his fellow cast members and his&nbsp;
experience on the hit CBS sitcom on the whole.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:30.880
"We're a family and we've got each&nbsp;
other's backs. We have from day one."

